technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Consonant Blends - The <span class=\"strong\">/tw/</span> Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Consonant clusters like /tw/ can occur at the beginning of a word in English. <br/><br/>Practice blending the sound from one consonant sound into the next without adding a vowel sound in between.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Read the following words aloud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twitter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tweet\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twist\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twin\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twig\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"tweak\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"twenty\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Here's a story for your Twitter feed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Now that's something to tweet about!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Breaking Sentences into Parts", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you read or speak in English, you often \u201cchunk\u201d or break the sentence into parts based on the meaning contained in each part.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example, look at the sentence: ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class =\"italic\">To fight the disease, Cousins decided to add a twist to traditional medical treatment. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This sentence could be chunked or broken into the following parts:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To fight the disease, <br/>Cousins decided <br/>to add a twist <br/>to traditional medical treatment. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To fight the disease, * Cousins decided * to add a twist * to traditional medical treatment. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "joint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "part of the body that bends, like at the finger, elbow or knee", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Arthritis causes people great pain as their joints become stiff.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about laughter and medicine.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "arthritis", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a disease affecting the movement of joints in the body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Arthritis is a disease that affects the joints of the body.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to be diagnosed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a health problem proven by medical tests", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Norman Cousins was diagnosed with a severe form of arthritis.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "add a twist", "type": "name"}, {"content": "change; alter is some way ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Cousins decided to add a twist to traditional medical treatment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "recovery", "type": "name"}, {"content": "improved health condition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Cousins was convinced that \"laughter therapy\" was the key to his recovery.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "dose", "type": "name"}, {"content": "amount taken, usually of a medication", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  A dose of Vitamin C allowed him two hours of painless sleep.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "humor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the ability to find things comical funny", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Cousins exposed himself to a steady diet of humor. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn7le02ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Go online to find 3 - 5 jokes in English. Make sure you understand the jokes and you think they are funny.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice saying the important words in each joke.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the jokes without reading them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell the jokes to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With your partner, decide which joke is the funniest.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I practice saying 3 - 5 jokes in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell the jokes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I decide which joke is the funniest.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "Here's a story for your Twitter feed. In 1964, Norman Cousins, the editor of one of the most popular magazines in America, the <span class =\"italic\">Saturday Review</span>, was told by his doctor that he only had a short time left to live. He was diagnosed with a severe form of arthritis that causes people great pain as their joints become increasingly stiff."}, {"image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg", "time": "23000", "id": 2, "text": "To fight the disease, Cousins decided to add a twist to traditional medical treatment. He took a lot of Vitamin C and exposed himself to a steady diet of humor. He soon found that ten minutes of energetic laughter and a dose of Vitamin C allowed him two hours of painless sleep, and the inflammation in his joints had decreased. Cousins was convinced that \"laughter therapy\" was the key to his recovery."}, {"image": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg", "time": "53000", "id": 3, "text": "Norman Cousins lived until the year 1990. By that time, he had become famous not only as a magazine editor but also as the discoverer of a new form of medical treatment. His book <span class=\"italic\">Anatomy of an Illness</span> persuaded many physicians to begin taking humor seriously as one means of improving their patients' health. Now that's something to tweet about!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le02ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le02ob04re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about staying healthy.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say and use the sound tw.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can use proper intonation in long statements. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you think the expression \u201claughter therapy\u201d means?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you take vitamins like Vitamin C? Why or why not? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"cont